---
import {
  ComputerTerminal01Icon,
  Key01Icon,
  LockKeyIcon,
  McpServerIcon,
} from '@hugeicons/core-free-icons'
import FeaturePage from '@/components/FeaturePage.astro'

const related = [
  { title: 'Hosted MCP', text: 'Connect seoskill.dev/mcp to Claude Code, Codex or any remote MCP client.', href: '/docs/mcp', icon: McpServerIcon },
  { title: 'CLI and local MCP', text: 'Install seo and add the local MCP server to your agents.', href: '/docs/cli', icon: ComputerTerminal01Icon },
  { title: 'API keys', text: 'Add DataForSEO or Ahrefs for keyword and competitor research.', href: '/docs/keys', icon: Key01Icon },
  { title: 'What is stored', text: 'What the hosted MCP and the CLI keep, and what they never keep.', href: '/docs/privacy', icon: LockKeyIcon },
]
---

<FeaturePage
  title="SEO MCP server for AI agents"
  description="Connect a free SEO MCP server to Claude, Codex, Cursor or any agent. Read Search Console, Google Analytics and keyword data. Your data and keys are never stored."
  path="/features/mcp"
  lead="Ask your agent what changed, what is broken and where the opportunities are. It reads your own search data before it answers."
  {related}
>
  <h2>Hosted or local, same tools</h2>
  <p>
    The hosted MCP at <code>https://seoskill.dev/mcp</code> needs nothing
    installed: add it to your agent and sign in with Google. The local MCP runs
    on your machine with the CLI. Run <code>seo mcp install</code> after setup
    to add it to your agents. Both serve the same tools, and the local one adds
    the site crawl and internal links.
  </p>

  <h2>The tools your agent gets</h2>
  <table>
    <thead><tr><th>Tool</th><th>What it returns</th></tr></thead>
    <tbody>
      <tr><td><code>seo_sites</code></td><td>The Search Console and Google Analytics properties you can read.</td></tr>
      <tr><td><code>seo_report</code></td><td>The main Search Console report: an overview, then one section.</td></tr>
      <tr><td><code>seo_page</code></td><td>One URL: live page facts, Google index status and its queries.</td></tr>
      <tr><td><code>seo_compare</code></td><td>Before and after a date, with Google updates in the window.</td></tr>
      <tr><td><code>seo_index</code></td><td>Pages that lost their clicks, checked live and with URL Inspection.</td></tr>
      <tr><td><code>seo_research</code></td><td>Keyword and competitor data from your DataForSEO or Ahrefs key.</td></tr>
      <tr><td><code>seo_data</code></td><td>Raw Search Console rows, or Google Analytics landing pages.</td></tr>
      <tr><td><code>seo_crawl</code>, <code>seo_internal_links</code></td><td>The site crawl and internal links. Local MCP only.</td></tr>
    </tbody>
  </table>

  <h2>What the hosted server keeps</h2>
  <p>
    Your data and keys are never stored. Your Google sign-in and any keys are
    sealed into the tokens your MCP client keeps, and the server uses them for
    one request at a time. The only thing kept is an anonymous count of what
    ran. <a href="/docs/privacy">What is stored</a> has the details.
  </p>
</FeaturePage>
